Q34: What does a CFAR detector do, in one or two sentences?
---
A Constant False Alarm Rate (CFAR) detector is a signal processing technique used in radar and communications to estimate the noise floor in the presence of interfering signals. It dynamically adjusts the detection threshold based on the local signal environment to maintain a constant probability of false alarms, ensuring reliable detection even when strong interferers are present.<|im_end|>
